workedExamples.question_text:
Water flows horizontally from a pipe $45\text{ m}$ above sea level and reaches the sea $18\text{ m}$ horizontally from the pipe. Taking the pipe as the origin, its equations are $x=Vt$ and $y=-5t^2$. Find its initial speed.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw (0,0) -- (0,3) -- (-0.5,3);
\draw (-0.5,0) -- (3.1,0);
\draw[->] (0,3) -- (1,3);
\path (1,3) node[above] {$V$};
\fill (0,3) circle (1.5pt);
\fill (2.4,0) circle (1.5pt);
\draw[<->] (-0.8,0) -- (-0.8,3);
\path (-0.8,1.5) node[left] {$45\,\mathrm{m}$};
\draw[<->] (0,-0.5) -- (2.4,-0.5);
\path (1.2,-0.5) node[below] {$18\,\mathrm{m}$};
\path (0,3) node[above left] {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A ball is projected from level ground at $45^{\circ}$ above the horizontal and just clears a wall $10\text{ m}$ high and $30\text{ m}$ away. Its equations are $x=Vt\cos45^{\circ}$ and $y=Vt\sin45^{\circ}-5t^2$. Find its initial speed to $1$ decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw (-0.3,0) -- (4.1,0);
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0.9,0.9);
\draw (0.55,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=45,radius=0.55];
\path (0.85,0.3) node {$45^{\circ}$};
\path (0.9,0.9) node[above left] {$V$};
\draw[thick] (3,0) -- (3,1);
\path (3,0.5) node[right] {$10\,\mathrm{m}$};
\draw[<->] (0,-0.5) -- (3,-0.5);
\path (1.5,-0.5) node[below] {$30\,\mathrm{m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A stone is thrown from a cliff $65\text{ m}$ above the sea at $45^{\circ}$ below the horizontal. It lands $20\text{ m}$ horizontally from the base. Taking the launch point as the origin, its equations are $x=Vt\cos45^{\circ}$ and $y=-Vt\sin45^{\circ}-5t^2$. Find its initial speed to $1$ decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw (-0.5,3) -- (0,3) -- (0,0);
\draw (-0.5,0) -- (3.1,0);
\draw[dashed] (0,3) -- (1.4,3);
\draw[->] (0,3) -- (0.9,2.1);
\draw (0.55,3) arc[start angle=0,end angle=-45,radius=0.55];
\path (0.95,2.7) node {$45^{\circ}$};
\path (0.9,2.1) node[below right] {$V$};
\fill (2.4,0) circle (1.5pt);
\draw[<->] (-0.8,0) -- (-0.8,3);
\path (-0.8,1.5) node[left] {$65\,\mathrm{m}$};
\draw[<->] (0,-0.5) -- (2.4,-0.5);
\path (1.2,-0.5) node[below] {$20\,\mathrm{m}$};
\path (0,3) node[above left] {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.question_text:
A football is kicked from level ground at $40^{\circ}$ to the horizontal and just clears a wall $5\text{ m}$ high standing $20\text{ m}$ away.
Taking $g=10\text{ m/s}^{2}$, find the speed of the kick to $1$ decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta, angles, quotes}
\draw (-0.4,0) -- (6.8,0);
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (1.8,0);
\coordinate (B) at (1.15,0.96);
\fill (O) circle (2pt);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (O) -- (B);
\pic[draw, "$40^{\circ}$", angle radius=0.8cm, angle eccentricity=1.7] {angle = A--O--B};
\draw[very thick] (5.6,0) -- (5.6,1.4) node[midway, right] {$5\text{ m}$};
\draw[|<->|] (0,-0.6) -- (5.6,-0.6) node[midway, below] {$20\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A ball is thrown at $25\text{ m/s}$ from a platform $10\text{ m}$ above level ground and lands $50\text{ m}$ from the base of the platform.
Taking the launch point as the origin and $g=10\text{ m/s}^{2}$, find the two possible angles of projection to $1$ decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta, angles, quotes}
\draw (0,1.2) -- (0.6,1.2) -- (0.6,0);
\draw (0,0) -- (7.2,0);
\coordinate (P) at (0.6,1.2);
\coordinate (H) at (1.9,1.2);
\coordinate (Q) at (1.65,1.8);
\coordinate (L) at (6.6,0);
\draw[dashed] (P) -- (H);
\fill (P) circle (2pt);
\fill (L) circle (2pt);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (P) -- (Q) node[pos=1, above right] {$25\text{ m/s}$};
\pic[draw, "$\theta$", angle radius=0.6cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle = H--P--Q};
\draw[|<->|] (0.6,-0.6) -- (6.6,-0.6) node[midway, below] {$50\text{ m}$};
\draw[gray] (0,0) -- (-0.7,0);
\draw[gray] (0,1.2) -- (-0.7,1.2);
\draw[|<->|] (-0.5,0) -- (-0.5,1.2) node[midway, left] {$10\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
